WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.556 --> 00:00:03.139
(somber music)

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:07.300
- Pre-COVID, I was really out there

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:10.040
with the people, with my family,

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:11.583
just staying involved.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:18.400
Loved to entertain, loved
to have people over.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.770
I'm a mother of four, grandmother of two.

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:25.563
Beautiful family, I love my
children and my grandchildren.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:32.330
I got ill, it was March 18th.

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:35.950
I got really scared
because I realized then

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:38.150
this stuff was in my body

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:40.440
and we didn't know anything about it

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.380
and the only thing that
I was hearing about COVID

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:45.513
was that people were dying from it.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:48.763
And I didn't want to die.

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:52.220
My expectation when recovering was

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:54.960
I would get better and
I would be done with it.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.443
And that's been furthest
from the truth for me.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:24.180
- I'm in a wheelchair going
anywhere more than five feet.

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:26.230
I'm pretty much bedridden.

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:31.170
I still have heart
issues, digestive issues,

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:34.050
headaches, dizziness, low blood pressure.

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:36.560
- I couldn't walk three or
four feet across a room.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.330
Full onset of asthma symptoms

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:41.640
where I was having two or
three asthma attacks a day.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:45.090
- I was athletic most of
my life prior to COVID.

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:47.723
I was working out and doing
high-intensity workouts.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.260
I'm just standing still talking

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:52.790
and my heart rate's up.

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:54.820
And this kind of goes in waves.

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:56.400
It waxes and wains.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:00.060
- The medical community thought
that this was one and done,

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:02.150
meaning if you survive the infection

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:03.980
that you would become normal

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:06.090
and this is definitely not the case now.

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:08.400
The other thing that I think is surprising

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:11.360
is how many organ systems that this virus

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:12.730
is actually effecting.

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:14.800
Pulmonary, meaning the lungs,

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:17.956
cardiac, the heart, neurological,

00:02:17.956 --> 00:02:21.223
and also psychological.

00:02:22.965 --> 00:02:25.163
- I can faintly smell it.

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:33.300
My post-COVID symptoms
that I've been experiencing

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:37.270
are loss of hair, loss of smell,

00:02:37.270 --> 00:02:40.460
of course memory fog, memory loss,

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:43.400
joint pains in different places.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.420
- We're at a loss as to what to do

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:48.640
for some of these patients
and their severe symptoms.

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:51.830
- What worries me the
most is the brain fog

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:56.480
because my father, he had Alzheimer's.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:59.160
I hoped and prayed that
I never would have to

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.530
go through that experience,

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:04.470
because I watched my father
go through that experience.

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:07.760
Not being able to speak as fast

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:10.350
and be as sharp as I used to,

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:15.070
that is definitely something
that is concerning to me.

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:18.840
- I was very fit and healthy
before I contracted the virus.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:22.300
Before the spring I was
with my partner's family

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:27.300
in Norway and we were hiking
up mountains on the west coast.

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:31.370
The most worrying thing
through all of this has been

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:33.430
they haven't been able to find a reason

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:35.413
for why I've been so poorly.

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:47.520
- I'm about to get on Zoom
with Pastor Robert Dixon.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:52.410
Post-COVID symptoms, how's
everything going with that?

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:54.130
How are you making it through?

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:57.030
- It's been a pleasure
just knowing somebody else.

00:03:57.030 --> 00:03:59.260
Like, you're not on an island by yourself.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:03.760
- When I saw you put your Facebook post up

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:07.630
about you dealing with
COVID and just the extent

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:09.920
of how you went into details,

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:12.700
it was really good to hear

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:16.160
and then it helped me
to be able to share more

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:18.040
about what I was dealing with.

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:19.730
- [Robert] If I'm in
the middle of a thought,

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:22.488
I can be thinking of a
word and just not get it.

00:04:22.488 --> 00:04:23.905
- That's me, yes!

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:28.550
- In regards to preventing
further decline,

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:31.380
I don't know if there's
anything that we can do,

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:34.270
mostly because I don't
think we understand enough

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:37.650
about the time course and the ideology,

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:39.130
or the cause of these symptoms.

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:41.853
I fear that they will
never get back to baseline.

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:45.610
We can't tell for now whether
that's a possibility or not.

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:49.380
- Just had a heart episode
coming down the stairs.

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:53.740
My heart hit 150 beats per minute.

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:54.840
I'm out of breath.

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:56.930
Another trip to urgent care.

00:04:56.930 --> 00:04:59.212
Waiting to find out if we're gonna have to

00:04:59.212 --> 00:05:00.710
go to the ER or not.

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:03.363
Had another heart episode
yesterday and this morning.

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:11.160
- Everything that I'm doing now

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:16.160
is to get my body, my mind
back to where I was before.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:21.460
I don't want to stay in the
place that I'm in right now,

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:23.200
because it's not a good place

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:26.690
mentally, emotionally or physically.

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:29.050
I exercise in the mornings.

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:33.410
I may not be able to do
the full 30-minute workout,

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:35.960
but I'll try to do
something just for the sake

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:39.867
of saying that I am
continuing working on my body.

00:05:39.867 --> 00:05:41.652
- [Physical Therapist]
Add some resistance.

00:05:41.652 --> 00:05:43.993
Breathe in and then breathe out.

00:05:43.993 --> 00:05:48.010
- I have retrain my lungs
how to breathe correctly.

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:50.840
Instead of taking shallow breaths,

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:52.974
I need to use my diaphragm and
my diaphragm's really weak,

00:05:52.974 --> 00:05:56.240
so PT is helping me.

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:59.020
- There will be more patients
with long-term symptoms,

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:01.040
so the need to understand the disease

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:03.450
is not only to treat the
patients we have now,

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:05.603
but also the patients for the future.

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:14.200
- The future for me with the
side effects that I'm having

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:17.800
is tomorrow, it's not a year later,

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:20.640
five years or 10 years later.

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:25.640
I'm trying my best to do
what I can within my power

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:30.223
with prayer, my faith
in God, to get better.

